course: dictionary
lesson: 14650
title: Things that must come first
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A precondition is something that must be true, or must happen, before something else can happen. The first part of the word, pre-, means before, so a precondition always comes first.
explain: «Having a ticket is a precondition for entering the show.» You cannot go in until you have a ticket. The ticket has to come before the show can start for you.
explain: Try the swap test. Put «something that must come first» in place of precondition: «Learning to count is something that must come first for learning to add.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Precondition means something that must be true, or must happen, before something else can happen.
fact: Pre- means before, so a precondition comes before.
fact: «Water is a precondition for life.» Living things cannot survive without water first.
fact: In rules and talks, «There are no preconditions for joining the club» means you do not need anything to happen first.
fact: In computing, a precondition is what must be true before a program step runs.
exercise: «Having a ticket is a precondition for entering the show.» What does precondition mean? | *Something that must happen before something else can | A seat in the theatre | Something that happens after the show | A reason to clap loudly
exercise: «Learning to count is a precondition for learning to add.» Which must come first? | Neither is needed | Learning to add | *Learning to count | They happen at the same time
exercise: Jayden says, «There are no preconditions for joining the club.» What does he mean? | You must be a member already | You must wear a club badge | You must pay money before you join | *Nothing has to happen first before you can join
test: Which sentence uses precondition correctly? | Precondition is my favourite colour | The precondition ran out of paint at the party | *Practising every day is a precondition for getting better at the piano
test: In precondition, what does pre- mean? | *Before | Again | After | Inside
exam: In computing, what is a precondition? | The screen that shows the answer | The last line of code in a program | A computer game with lots of levels | *What must be true before a program step runs
